            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Brunn W. Roysdon, Solicitor General), according to Petitioner (Brunn W. Roysdon, Solicitor General), the petition framed the case as a question of statutory interpretation, arguing that \u00a7\u202f2254(e)(2) creates a high bar for federal evidentiary hearings on habeas claims involving state convictions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "342187631083a1b5b4d1afbb03b84830fefcfb944b33539ae80731feebce5105",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-342187631083-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 15,
              "start": 15
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, the Court needed to determine what \u201cat fault\u201d means under \u00a7\u202f2254(e)(2)."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Background & Question",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "case_id": "2021-20-1009",
  "decision": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "131ee37282b85402b6da9743e1b6479ee2c4d36d313f18cfad9a80cecce21899",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-131ee37282b8-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court interpreted \u201cfail\u201d to mean that the prisoner must be at fault for the undeveloped record in state court."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "131ee37282b85402b6da9743e1b6479ee2c4d36d313f18cfad9a80cecce21899",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-131ee37282b8-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that attorney negligence is chargeable to the client and bars relief unless the conditions of \u00a7\u202f2254(e)(2) are satisfied."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "131ee37282b85402b6da9743e1b6479ee2c4d36d313f18cfad9a80cecce21899",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-131ee37282b8-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor\u2019s dissent contended that the majority overstates the harm to states that would result from allowing prisoners to develop evidence outside the narrow exceptions of \u00a7\u202f2254(e)(2)."
      }
    ],
